.Dd February 11, 2026
.Dt CPIO 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cpio
.Nd cpio archive formats
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This document describes cpio formats supported by
.Xr cpio 1 :
.Pp
.Bl -bullet
.It
newc (SVR4 ASCII header, magic 070701)
.It
crc (newc with magic 070702; its last header field, zero in newc, is the
sum of the bytes of a regular file's data, modulo 2^32)
.It
odc (portable old character format, magic 070707)
.It
bin (old binary format, magic 070707 in a 16-bit word).
Its words are in the byte order of the machine that wrote it;
.Xr cpio 1
writes its own (little-endian on x86) and reads either.
.El
.Pp
Each archive entry contains a header, pathname, file payload (if any), and
format-specific alignment padding.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cpio 1 ,
.Xr pax 1
